# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mustr — deploy-time secrets.
#
# The "Deploy to Cloudflare" button reads this file to know what to prompt you
# for during setup. For LOCAL development, copy this file to .dev.vars (which is
# gitignored) and fill in the values. In production, the deploy flow stores
# these as encrypted Worker secrets — you never commit real values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED — a long random password YOU invent. It unlocks the one-time setup
# wizard the first time your site loads, so a random passer-by can't claim your
# site before you do. You'll paste it once in the wizard, then it's done.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 24
SETUP_TOKEN=

# REQUIRED — 32+ random bytes used to sign login/session cookies.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL — leave these blank and enter them in the setup wizard instead
# (recommended; the wizard walks you through where to find them). They come
# from your Discord application:
#   Client Secret  →  Discord app → OAuth2 → Reset Secret
#   Bot Token      →  Discord app → Bot → Reset Token
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
